"notes": ["Source: Lions 2026 media guide, 'INDIVIDUAL RECORDS' section, pdf pp. 326-334 (printed page numbers equal pdf page numbers); every list is a titled table with Rank, Player, stat columns and Years/Year or Opp/Date, top 5 for career and season (more for game lists and ties). Postseason individual records (pdf pp. 343-345), opponent records and team records were not used.","through_season 2025: the tables include 2025-season entries (Jack Campbell 166 tackles in 2025, Jahmyr Gibbs and Jared Goff 2025 games, Aidan Hutchinson 14.5 sacks in 2025); players still on the roster are printed in blue with an open-ended Years like '2021-'.","Method: every row was read from 220-300 dpi crops of the page pictures; the IA OCR of this guide is poor (columns come out in separate runs, many digits wrong), so the pictures were the primary reading. All career and season rows with companion columns were then checked arithmetically and agree with the printed numbers: yards per attempt/reception/return average = Yds / Att, Rec or Int, passer rating and completion percentage recomputed from Att/Cmp/Yds/TD/Int, and tackles TT = ST + AT. Ranks are as printed (the guide prints rank numbers, with 't' after a tied rank; ties therefore skip the next rank, e.g. 1t,1t,3). complete_to counts printed rows, not rank numbers. raw keeps the printed columns in printed order (comma grouping as printed: some tables print 15,269, others 15269).","Game rows: the table columns are Opp and Date; `years` holds the date followed by the printed opponent code. The 'INTERCEPTIONS, GAME' table prints its header as 'Int, Date, Opp' but the columns hold opponent then date.","Sacks: the guide prints two lists per scope under 'Sacks': 'QUARTERBACK SACKS ... (OFFICIAL SACKS SINCE 1982)' and, just below it, 'Unofficial totals including sacks from 1973-81 published in previous versions of Lions Media Guides' (Al \"Bubba\" Baker 75.5 etc.). Both are transcribed as separate lists with the same scope/category (career, season and game), official first; the unofficial ones carry the words 'unofficial totals including sacks from 1973-81' in title and scope_note.","Tackles: unofficial statistic compiled since 1973 per the guide's footnote under the tackles tables; no solo/assist split is printed for Ken Fantetti and Doug English.","Printing inconsistencies in non-ranking columns (no effect on any `value`): the TD column for Johnnie Morton is 21 in the RECEPTIONS, CAREER table but 35 in RECEIVING YARDS, CAREER and RECEIVING TOUCHDOWNS, CAREER; for Herman Moore it is 61 in RECEIVING YARDS, CAREER and 62 elsewhere.","Date conflict kept as printed and flagged uncertain: PASSING YARDS, GAME rank 8 (Matthew Stafford, 422 yards vs Cle) is dated 11/11/2009 while PASSING TOUCHDOWNS, GAME prints Stafford vs Cle on 11/22/2009; the value 422 is clearly legible.","Partial tie groups: game rush_td (2t group of 19), game rec_td (3t group of 21), game int (2t group of 16) and game pass_td (8t group of 27) are only partly transcribed, as stated in each scope_note; rows are in printed order and every transcribed row of such a group carries tie=true."]
}
